  m_Name: Jom_W13_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Jom
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d01af24494056374182e13118c0585e2, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'Mariknam kadi ti angot dayta a mapudpudot a longganisa? Napno ti
    counterko!


    No kasapulam a tawagan iti naurnos a wagas ti panagkitana ti
    maysa a tao wenno lumabas iti napno a lugar, mabalinmo nga ibaga ti ''dispensaren
    nak.''


    Kayatna a saoen ti ''excuse me.''


    Denggem a naimbag: dispensaren
    nak.


    Ita, padasem nga ibagam ti ''dispensaren nak'' iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'Smell that sizzling longganisa? My counter is getting crowded!

    When
    you need to politely get someone''s attention or pass through a crowded space,
    you can say ''dispensaren nak.''

    It means ''excuse me.''

    Now, try saying
    ''dispensaren nak'' yourself.'
